{
  "requirement": "Criteria obtain the agent selected by the domain's validation cache through\ntheir `ValidationContext`. The application supplies the configuration under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`. The SDK does not persist it.\nA cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.deterministic_procedures`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests check each obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`.\n\n**1. Criteria get the agent selected by the domain's cache through their `ValidationContext`.**\n- `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors` in `agent/configured.rs` builds a domain from `ValidationCache::with_agent(config)`. It runs `validation::verify` with an asking criterion. The missing-credential error names the configured env var, so the request used the cache's agent.\n- It also asserts that the provider stays uninitialized until a criterion awaits a request.\n- `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` and `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat` run criteria against local servers. The model, endpoint and key the application supplied appear in the requests the servers receive.\n- `bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted` asserts with `Arc::ptr_eq` that a clone of the domain shares the cache's agent. It also asserts that the agent's config equals the supplied config.\n- `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` in `agent/tests.rs` covers criteria asking through an agent.\n- `supported_backend_settings_create_transports_without_sending_requests` in `agent/providers.rs` covers the supplied configurations producing transports.\n\n**2. The application supplies the configuration.** That clause cites `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`, which has its own tests. Every test above supplies configuration this way.\n\n**3. The SDK does not persist the configuration.**\n- The Bedrock test serializes the stored evidence record. It asserts there is no `backend` key and no profile or model strings.\n- The OpenAI test does this after each of two runs. It asserts the saved JSON contains none of `local-transport-key`, `local-test`, `backend` or `api_key`.\n\n**4. A cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria.**\n- `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` in `agent/tests.rs` runs a deterministic criterion on `Memory`. `Memory` has a `cache` field and no agent is installed. The test asserts the computed output and the recorded dependency.\n- `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` in `graph/validation_tests.rs` shows the other side. With no agent, an asking criterion yields `NoAgentConfigured` and stores nothing.\n- The deterministic criterion inside the configured test also runs without initializing the provider.\n\nI found no obligation that lacks a test. The gaps I checked for all have tests that would catch them:\n- A criterion ignoring the cache's agent would fail the configured-agent tests.\n- Persisting the configuration would fail the saved-JSON assertions.\n- Deterministic criteria needing an agent would fail the no-agent test.",
  "references": "a7c327df3723dd097da425415d02491ba38f1398e61cad8e250b6b3934e6537e",
